# @Environment

Reads values the system or an ancestor passes down, like dark mode or the locale.

Also called: useContext, React Context, provide inject, prop drilling, dark mode, theme, dependency injection, traitCollection, global value, @EnvironmentObject.

## Contents

- Default code
- Pitfalls
- Key APIs
- Variants
- Related

## Default code

```swift
@Environment(\.colorScheme) private var colorScheme

var body: some View {
    Text(colorScheme == .dark ? "Good night" : "Good morning")
}
```

**Note:** It works like React's `useContext`: any view reads what an ancestor or the system set, without props through every layer.

## Pitfalls

- **Values flow down, never up.** `.environment(\.key, value)` changes a value for that view and everything inside it, not for parents or siblings. `.font()`, `.tint()`, and `.disabled()` work the same way.
- **Mark environment properties `private`.** The view reads them itself; nobody passes them in.
- **A missing model crashes.** `@Environment(Model.self)` stops the app if no ancestor called `.environment(model)`. Declare it as `Model?` when it might be absent. See @Observable (`observable`).

## Key APIs

- `@Environment(\.colorScheme)`: Reads a system value. Others: `dismiss`, `locale`, `openURL`.
- `.environment(\.key, value)`: Overrides a value for a view and its children.
- `@Entry var name = default`: Adds your own value, inside `extension EnvironmentValues`.
- `.environment(model)`: Shares an `@Observable` model with every view below.
- `@Environment(Model.self)`: Reads that model back by its type.

## Variants

### Close a sheet with dismiss

Read `dismiss` inside a sheet to close it, without a binding from the parent.

```swift
struct ContentView: View {
    @State private var isShowingSheet = false

    var body: some View {
        Button("Open sheet") { isShowingSheet = true }
            .buttonStyle(.borderedProminent)
            .sheet(isPresented: $isShowingSheet) {
                SheetContent()
            }
    }
}

struct SheetContent: View {
    @Environment(\.dismiss) private var dismiss

    var body: some View {
        VStack(spacing: 16) {
            Text("All set!")
                .font(.title2.bold())
            Button("Done") { dismiss() }
                .buttonStyle(.borderedProminent)
        }
        .presentationDetents([.height(200)])
    }
}
```

**Note:** Some environment values are actions you call like functions, such as `dismiss()` and `openURL(url)`.

### Your own value with @Entry

Declare a value with `@Entry`, set it once with `.environment`, and read it any number of levels down.

```swift
extension EnvironmentValues {
    @Entry var cardTint: Color = .blue
}

struct ContentView: View {
    @State private var tint = Color.blue

    var body: some View {
        VStack(spacing: 16) {
            Picker("Tint", selection: $tint) {
                Text("Blue").tag(Color.blue)
                Text("Pink").tag(Color.pink)
                Text("Green").tag(Color.green)
            }
            .pickerStyle(.segmented)
            ActionBar()
        }
        .environment(\.cardTint, tint)
    }
}

struct ActionBar: View {
    var body: some View {
        HStack {
            ActionButton(symbol: "heart.fill")
            ActionButton(symbol: "star.fill")
            ActionButton(symbol: "bookmark.fill")
        }
    }
}

struct ActionButton: View {
    let symbol: String
    @Environment(\.cardTint) private var tint

    var body: some View {
        Image(systemName: symbol)
            .font(.title2)
            .foregroundStyle(.white)
            .frame(width: 56, height: 56)
            .background(tint.gradient, in: .rect(cornerRadius: 14))
    }
}
```

**Note:** `ActionBar` never mentions the tint. Only `ActionButton`, two levels down, reads it.

### Respect Reduce Motion

Read `accessibilityReduceMotion` and skip bouncy or zooming animations for people who turned it on.

```swift
@Environment(\.accessibilityReduceMotion) private var reduceMotion
@State private var isLiked = false

var body: some View {
    Button {
        withAnimation(reduceMotion ? nil : .bouncy) {
            isLiked.toggle()
        }
    } label: {
        Image(systemName: isLiked ? "heart.fill" : "heart")
            .font(.largeTitle)
            .foregroundStyle(.pink)
            .scaleEffect(isLiked ? 1.3 : 1)
    }
    .accessibilityLabel(isLiked ? "Unlike" : "Like")
}
```

**Note:** Other accessibility settings live here too, such as `accessibilityReduceTransparency` and `dynamicTypeSize`.

## Related

`observable`, `choosing-wrappers`, `binding`, `sheet`

